dia, or direct rule in India. The region under British control was commonly called India in contemporaneous usage and included areas directly administered by the United Kingdom, which were collectively called British India, and areas ruled by indigenous rulers, but under British paramountcy, called the princely states. The region was sometimes called the Indian Empire, though not officially."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q129286","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q1348","value_label":"Kolkata","from_t":1858,"to_t":1911,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Kolkata"},{"qid":"Q129286","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q987","value_label":"New Delhi","from_t":1911,"to_t":1947,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"New Delhi"},{"qid":"Q129286","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q1860","value_label":"English","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"English"},{"qid":"Q129286","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q1860","value_label":"English","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"English"},{"qid":"Q129286","kind":"official_religion","value_qid":"Q9089","value_label":"Hinduism","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P3075","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Hinduism"},{"qid":"Q129286","kind":"official_religion","value_qid":"Q432","value_label":"Islam","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P3075","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Islam"},{"qid":"Q129286","kind":"official_religion","value_qid":"Q9316","value_label":"Sikhism","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P3075","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Sikhism"},{"qid":"Q129286","kind":"official_religion","value_qid":"Q748","value_label":"Buddhism","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P3075","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Buddhism"},{"qid":"Q129286","kind":"official_religion","value_qid":"Q5043","value_label":"Christianity","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null